Package: swapspace
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: dynamic swap space manager
 Swapspace watches memory usage and creates swap files in a dedicated
 directory when the system needs more virtual memory, then removes them
 again once the pressure is gone. This avoids sizing a swap partition
 in advance.
 .
 The systemd unit is installed but neither enabled nor started; enable it
 with "systemctl enable --now swapspace".
